{"parentUuid":"c0583fa7-449f-4ad9-b669-02d55f97c689","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"52265f9a-6091-4f5a-9e76-21d47572f3d8","agentId":"af4ae0306e46b6e08","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G83fHLkidGQQheQCjjDMsP","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"The FLUX.2 edit that made FluXray, as a record, and the rules of its reproduction.\n\nThe owner's ask of 2026-10-25: find CSAIL's trained Flux Realism and finetune it until it makes\nX-rays numerically indistinguishable from FleXray's Hugging Face dataset, resolution first. What\nCSAIL released is no trained model: FluXray (the \"Enhanced DRRs\" of arXiv 2609.26756, FleXray's\npaper) is FLUX.2 [klein] 9B used as it ships, zero-shot, on raw DRRs rendered from the MOOSE CTs,\nwith one prompt, four denoising steps and two filters, and the paper says it \"needs no\ntask-specific fine-tuning\". So the reproducible object is the recipe, kept here word for word,\nand the finetune is ours: a LoRA edit adapter on a klein model trained on (raw DRR, target)\npairs, whose target is FluXray itself, an edit by the 9B model or, where pairs exist, a real\nframe. This module holds what needs no torch and no network, so the gate proves it and the tools\nand the grid job read one copy:\n\n- the recipe: the prompt as the paper prints it, the model, the steps, the guidance, the\n  rendering geometry (1024 pixels, SDD 1250 mm, 0.6 mm pixels, the volume's centre as isocentre),\n  the 90 fixed poses (three source heights, six vertical offsets, five rotations about the long\n  axis) and the two filters (the foreground floor and the paired soft-Dice rule);\n- the models a finetune may start from, each with its licence and whether its weights are gated,\n  since the FLUX Non-Commercial License (9B, base-9B) and Apache 2.0 (4B, base-4B) decide what\n  the project may own (docs/research/flux-realism/README.md);\n- the filter rule as a function, so the tool and the tests agree on the cut-off;\n- the resolution arithmetic: what a pixel spans at the isocentre under each pose, what an\n  endplate's angle is quantised to at 256 and 1024 pixels, which is what the review's \"256 x 256\n  masks are too coarse for measurement\" means in degrees;\n- the pre-registered words of the comparison (matched, indistinguishable, undecided, separable)\n  and the rule that chooses one from the two-sample classifier's interval and the MMD's p-value,\n  fixed here before any number exists;\n- the LoRA training configuration, every hyperparameter named once, which tools/realism.py writes\n  for the trainer so a run is reproducible from this file and a seed;\n- the stages of the grid word `realism <stage>` (grid/gate.sh, grid/realism.sbatch), each one job;\n- the replication's plan (ReplicationPlan): the model, how the CTs and their poses are drawn by\n  seed, the arms, the statistics' sizes, and the lines of PREREG.md's frozen block that the flow\n  (flows/realism.py) holds the code to before it runs.\n\nResolution comes first: FluXray is stored at 256 pixels, which is FleXray's inference canvas and\nnot the data's limit, so the edit here runs at the model's native 1024 and keeps the renderer's\nexact 1024-pixel masks beside every image; the comparison to FluXray goes through FleXray's own\n256-pixel preprocessing, since that is the only size FluXray exists at.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport hashlib\nimport math\nfrom collections.abc import Callable, Sequence\nfrom dataclasses import asdict, dataclass\nfrom typing import TypedDict\n\nfrom beartype import beartype\nfrom beethoven_qa.contracts import ensure, require\n\n# The prompt, as the paper prints it over six lines (arXiv 2609.26756, the FluXray section); the\n# third and fourth lines are one sentence. Kept verbatim, since a reproduction that changes a\n# word is another experiment.\nPROMPT_LINES = (\n    \"Make this synthetic X-ray (generated by a projection through a CT) look like a real X-ray.\",\n    \"The generated image should preserve ALL anatomical structure, no shape changes at all.\",\n    \"Add a small amount of clinical text to the image typical of X-rays but do not change the\"\n    \" position\",\n    \"or location of the anatomy at all.\",\n    \"Also, add some realistic X-ray textures to the image.\",\n    \"The output must be well registered with the input.\",\n)\nPROMPT = \" \".join(PROMPT_LINES)\n\n# The fixed poses of the FluXray render: the source's distance from the isocentre along the\n# patient's anterior axis (y, mm), the detector's offset along the long axis (z, mm) and the\n# rotation about that axis (alpha, degrees); x, beta and gamma are 0. Three by six by five.\nPOSE_Y_MM = (650, 900, 1150)\nPOSE_Z_MM = (-300, -200, -100, 0, 100, 200)\nPOSE_ALPHA_DEG = (0, 45, -45, 90, -90)\n\n# Which klein a finetune starts from. Weights under the FLUX Non-Commercial License are gated on\n# the Hub (the owner accepts the licence there before any fetch); the project owns the output of\n# a finetune only where the licence allows it, so 4B is the one route whose weights it may keep.\nMODELS = {\n    \"klein-9b\": {\n        \"repo\": \"black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-9B\",\n        \"parameters_b\": 9,\n        \"distilled\": True,\n        \"licence\": \"FLUX Non-Commercial License\",\n        \"gated\": True,\n        \"commercial\": False,\n        \"toolkit_arch\": \"flux2_klein_9b\",\n        \"role\": \"the paper's model: the zero-shot replication and the teacher of a distilled edit\",\n    },\n    \"klein-4b\": {\n        \"repo\": \"black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-4B\",\n        \"parameters_b\": 4,\n        \"distilled\": True,\n        \"licence\": \"Apache-2.0\",\n        \"gated\": False,\n        \"commercial\": True,\n        \"toolkit_arch\": \"flux2_klein_4b\",\n        \"role\": \"the zero-shot edit the project may own, and the base of a distilled-model LoRA\",\n    },\n    \"klein-base-9b\": {\n        \"repo\": \"black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-base-9B\",\n        \"parameters_b\": 9,\n        \"distilled\": False,\n        \"licence\": \"FLUX Non-Commercial License\",\n        \"gated\": True,\n        \"commercial\": False,\n        \"toolkit_arch\": \"flux2_klein_9b\",\n        \"role\": \"the undistilled 9B, for a LoRA whose output stays non-commercial\",\n    },\n    \"klein-base-4b\": {\n        \"repo\": \"black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-base-4B\",\n        \"parameters_b\": 4,\n        \"distilled\": False,\n        \"licence\": \"Apache-2.0\",\n        \"gated\": False,\n        \"commercial\": True,\n        \"toolkit_arch\": \"flux2_klein_4b\",\n        \"role\": \"the undistilled 4B: the finetune's default base, the one whose weights the\"\n        \" project may keep\",\n    },\n}\nDEFAULT_BASE = \"klein-base-4b\"\n\n# The stages of the grid word `realism <stage>`, each one GPU job (grid/realism.sbatch), in the\n# order they depend on one another; none runs before the owner's word and count.\nSTAGES = (\"edit\", \"stats\", \"lora\", \"eval\")\nSTAGE_CLASS = {\"edit\": \"gpu\", \"stats\": \"gpu\", \"lora\": \"gpu\", \"eval\": \"gpu\"}\nSTAGE_WHAT = {\n    \"edit\": \"the paper's recipe run as it stands: raw DRRs at FluXray's recorded poses, edited\"\n    \" zero-shot at 1024 pixels, filtered as the paper filters\",\n    \"stats\": \"the metric suite of the kept edits and of the raw DRRs against FluXray at the same\"\n    \" samples, with FluXray's split-half null and the seed arms read apart\",\n    \"lora\": \"the LoRA edit adapter trained on the (raw DRR, target) pairs from the configuration\"\n    \" this module writes\",\n    \"eval\": \"the adapter's edits scored as the zero-shot edits were, seed by seed, against the\"\n    \" same null\",\n}\n\n# The words of the comparison, fixed before any number (the sibling study,\n# docs/research/drr-domain-gap/,\n# reads the same tests). A two-sample classifier's AUC of 0.5 is chance; its bootstrap interval is\n# read at both ends. MMD's permutation p-value below 0.05 says the samples differ.\nVERDICTS = (\"matched\", \"indistinguishable\", \"undecided\", \"separable\")\nCHANCE_AUC = 0.5\nINDISTINGUISHABLE_AUC = 0.6\nMMD_ALPHA = 0.05\n# The geometry check's bar: the median phase-correlation shift, in pixels of FleXray's 256 canvas,\n# between a raw render and FluXray's image of the same sample (PREREG.md, section 4).\nGEOMETRY_SHIFT_PX = 1.0\n\n\nclass Model(TypedDict):\n    repo: str\n    parameters_b: int\n    distilled: bool\n    licence: str\n    gated: bool\n    commercial: bool\n    toolkit_arch: str\n    role: str\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass EditRecipe:\n    \"\"\"The FluXray edit; the defaults are the paper's, so a recipe that names nothing is theirs.\"\"\"\n\n    model: str = \"klein-9b\"\n    steps: int = 4\n    guidance: float = 1.0\n    dtype: str = \"bfloat16\"\n    prompt: str = PROMPT\n    render_pixels: int = 1024\n    render_sdd_mm: float = 1250.0\n    render_spacing_mm: float = 0.6\n    isocentre: str = \"volume-centre\"\n    stored_pixels: int = 256\n    foreground_floor: float = 0.05\n    filter_quantile: float = 0.98\n    lora: str = \"\"\n\n\nFLUXRAY = EditRecipe()\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass LoraPlan:\n    \"\"\"Every hyperparameter of the LoRA edit finetune, named once; the defaults are the\n    pre-registered run.\"\"\"\n\n    base: str = DEFAULT_BASE\n    rank: int = 16\n    alpha: int = 16\n    learning_rate: float = 1e-4\n    steps: int = 2000\n    batch_size: int = 1\n    resolution: int = 1024\n    optimizer: str = \"adamw8bit\"\n    schedule: str = \"cosine\"\n    save_every: int = 250\n    seed: int = 20261025\n    target: str = \"fluxray\"\n\n\nLORA_TARGETS = (\"fluxray\", \"teacher\", \"real\")","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"1c9f7585-7b97-4a84-a2c9-0ec76c9c9315","timestamp":"2026-10-30T18:14:28.130Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e04638c6-4e5a-4a37-aa9a-7261880a83b1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/home/user/bordercall","root":"/home/user/bordercall","branch":"claude/project-thread-gv744i","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":3,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":6},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"OpenSpineConsortium/bordercall","visibility":"unknown"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"OpenSpineConsortium/bordercall","visibility":"unknown"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"OpenSpineConsortium/symphony-template","visibility":"unknown"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"OpenSpineConsortium/bordercall","visibility":"unknown"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"OpenSpineConsortium/SchwingNet","visibility":"unknown"}]}},"live_cwd":"/home/user/bordercall","platform":"linux"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c0583fa7-449f-4ad9-b669-02d55f97c689","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_projects","cwd":"/home/user/bordercall","sessionId":"cbdcd57f-bcf8-5a71-ab64-4f0b9fbdb74f","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"zany-kindling-liskov"}
